// Phase 6: ?{} inside for loop — Tier 2 hoist candidate (§8.10)
//
// EXPECTED-ERROR fixture (was: "Should compile clean; the batch planner may
// rewrite"). That header stopped being true when PR #508 landed
// E-EACH-BODY-DECL-UNSUPPORTED: the `let posts = ?{...}.all()` below sits inside
// an `<each>` body interpolation, and §17.7.3 scopes the each body to the `@.`
// sigil + an optional `as` alias, NOT author-declared locals. The rejection is
// correct on the merits — the decl was being DROPPED, so the `${posts.length}`
// on the row template dangled and the whole list rendered empty with no
// diagnostic. The comment is corrected here rather than the shape being
// rewritten, because rewriting it would delete the §8.10 probe: see the OPEN
// TENSION note in docs/changes/tool-import-prune-2026-08-11/progress.md — a
// per-row `?{}` (the Tier-2 hoist candidate this fixture exists to exercise)
// needs a per-row local to bind its result, which §17.7.3 forbids. Resolving
// that is a design ruling, not a sample edit.

< db src="./test.db" tables="users, posts">
${
  let users = ?{`SELECT id, name FROM users`}.all()
}
<ul>
  <each in=users as user>
    ${
      let posts = ?{`SELECT title FROM posts WHERE user_id = ${user.id}`}.all()
    }
    <li>${user.name} — ${posts.length} posts</>
  </each>
</ul>
</>
